    let toks: Vec<CTok> =
        word.chars().filter_map(|c| CTok::parse(&c.to_string())).collect();
    check::word_verdict(&toks).0
};
format!(
    "{turn}  gate {verdict}  → {}",
    if verdict == 'F' { "REFUSED" } else { "ADMITTED" }
);
```
This is the single most important pattern for a parallel-module plan: vita.rs branches on whether the word contains tri-valued glyphs (`∈ ∋ ~ ≁`) and dispatches either to `imasm16_3::parse_glyph_word` + `tri_ancestral_verdict` (SIXTEEN_3) or to `check::word_verdict` (classic Belnap-FOUR `check` module) — the two verdict engines are used side-by-side, gated by glyph content, never merged into one flow-graph evaluator.

## 6. `imasm_core::check` re-export / usage check

- `src/Cargo.toml` (mOMonadOS root) declares only one dependency edge to the shared crate:
```toml
imasm_core = { path = "../MoDoT/imasm_core", default-features = false }
```
(so the actual `imasm_core` implementation consumed by mOMonadOS's build lives at `/home/mrnob0dy666/imsgct/MoDoT/imasm_core/src/`, **not** any of the `momonados-proof-2026-08-*` copies, which are separate/older proof snapshots each with their own bundled `imasm_core`.)
- There is **no** re-export of `imasm_core::check` anywhere under `src/` (no `pub use imasm_core::check` found by search).
- However, `imasm_core::check` **is** directly imported and used from three files in `src/`:
```
src/vita.rs:26:use imasm_core::check;
src/sk_forge.rs:37:use imasm_core::check;
src/prooflift.rs:18:use imasm_core::check;
```
All three additionally import `use imasm_core::classic::Token as CTok;` alongside it, and (per vita.rs line 526) call only `check::word_verdict(&toks)`.
- The specific items named in the question — `Graph` (struct, `check.rs:24`), `frobenius_closures` (method on `Graph`, `check.rs:162`), `match_pairs` (free fn, `check.rs:322`), `from_sequence` (free fn, `check.rs:343`) — **do not appear anywhere in `src/`** (grep for `Graph\b|frobenius_closures|match_pairs|from_sequence` across `src/*.rs` returns zero real hits; the only `Graph` matches are unrelated doc-comment/string uses like "Graph-execution kernel" in kernel.rs and "Token Graph" in manus.rs).
- Conclusion: mOMonadOS's own side has touched `imasm_core::check` only through its lowest-level convenience function `word_verdict`, in exactly 3 files (vita.rs, sk_forge.rs, prooflift.rs). The graph/closure-analysis surface of `check` (`Graph`, `frobenius_closures`, `match_pairs`, `from_sequence`) has never been imported or called from mOMonadOS — confirming the prior investigation's claim, with the refinement that `check::word_verdict` (not just `imasm16_3`) has in fact been touched.
